{{Quote|Perhaps you failed to pay attention to the Senate orientation. They should have explained that Toydaria is a neutral system.|Katuunko, King of Toydaria, to Bail Organa|<ref name="Supply Lines" />}}
'''Toydaria''' was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Toydarian]] [[species]], located in [[Hutt Space]].

==Description==
A [[planet]] of the [[Toydaria system]] located in [[Hutt Space]],<ref name="GoD" /> Toydaria was a temperate world of [[forest]]s and [[swamp]]s,<ref name="DB" /> with mats of [[algae]] covering large portions of the planet's surface.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> The [[atmosphere]] was typically foggy, and carried a [[Color|greenish]] hue.<ref name="DB" /> [[N'Omis flower]]s grew on the planet.<ref name="CL" />

Toydaria was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Toydarian]]s,<ref name="DB" /> who created muck nests and lived in the atmosphere of muck lakes. Members of the [[species]] lived in clans, where a [[Toydarian clan bell]] could signify a noble family,<ref name="CL" /> and during the last [[Standard decade|decades]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="Supply Lines" /> and [[Galactic Empire]], Toydaria was governed by a [[Politics|feudal monarchy]], the [[Toydarian kingdom]], and was dominated by the [[Toydarian royalty]]. It exported consumables and labor, while importing other consumables and technology.<ref name="GoD" /> Some Toydarian [[City|cities]] on the surface of Toydaria were large enough to be visible from [[Realspace|space]]. Monsoons also large enough to be visible from space could form on the world.<ref name="VE" />

==History==
===Republic Era===
====Ryloth campaign====
In the last decades of the [[Galactic Republic]], the neutral [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] planet of Toydaria was governed by a monarchy. During the [[Clone Wars]], a galactic war between the Republic and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], [[King]] [[Katuunko]] of Toydaria, who was the current monarch, refused to support either factions, therefore making his planet strategically interested by the two warring governments. However, after a [[The Matter of Using Toydarian Territory to Aid the Shipment of Relief Supplies to the Citizens of Ryloth|diplomatic mission]] conducted by both [[Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] and [[Junior Representative]] [[Jar Jar Binks]] and opposed by Senator [[Lott Dod]] of the [[Trade Federation]], which involved the Republic using Toydarian soil as a staging area to send relief supplies to the [[Battle of Ryloth|war-torn]] [[Twi'lek]]s of [[Ryloth]] with permission from the Toydarian king, Katuunko decided to support the Republic.<ref name="Supply Lines" />

====Death of King Katuunko====
Later on in the war, Separatist leader [[Count]] [[Dooku]] ordered his new assassin [[Savage Opress]] to [[Showdown at Toydaria|capture]] King Katuunko alive, otherwise he would be severely punished. However, the mission went downhill after [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] intercepted Opress on Toydaria, resulting in him [[Death|killing]] Katuunko out of rage, angering Dooku in the process and being severely punished with [[Force lightning]].<ref name="WOTM">{{TCW|Witches of the Mist}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
[[File:SWU-Turbolaser-Salvo.png|thumb|230px|right|A Gladiator Star Destroyer attacks Toydaria]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], a [[Gladiator-class Star Destroyer|''Gladiator''-class Star Destroyer]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] attacked the [[Royal City (Toydaria)|Royal City]] of Toydaria, with a salvo of [[turbolaser]] fire hitting a [[deflector shield]] that the Royal City activated in its defense.<ref name="Turbolaser Salvo">{{SWU|set=Jump to Lightspeed|cardname=Turbolaser Salvo|link=8174214418}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Toydaria first appeared in "[[Supply Lines]]," an episode of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''<ref name="Supply Lines" /> that first aired on [[September 24]], [[2010]].<ref name="Supply Lines Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode303.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Supply Lines}}</ref>

